.TH SURFACE-C24 1 2026-10-30 "libsurface" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
surface-c24 \- drive a Digidesign Control|24 through libsurface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B surface-c24
.RB [ \-\-helper
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-fifo
.IR path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B surface-c24
listens on every network interface for a Control|24's announce, attaches the first desk it
hears, and drives it through libsurface: it labels the strips F1 to F24, mirrors each fader's
position onto its own meter, and prints every event the desk sends (the desk appearing, going
online or offline, fader moves, touches and releases, keys, V-Pot and jog turns, warnings).
A fader the hand leaves stays where it was left; a new session repaints the whole desk.
.PP
It holds no capability of its own: the packet socket comes from
.BR diginet-packet-helper (1),
which opens it with
.B cap_net_raw
and hands it over.
.PP
On
.B quit
it writes "OFF " on every scribble strip, waits for the desk to take it, and sends the
disconnect frame. A Control|24 that booted while other traffic flooded its link may ignore
every host; it is reported as a warning, and a power cycle on a quiet link brings it back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-helper " path"
The
.B diginet-packet-helper
to take the packet socket from. By default the one in
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BI \-\-fifo " path"
Read write commands from this FIFO, one per line; it is created when missing.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.SH FIFO COMMANDS
Strips are numbered 1 to 24.
.TP
.BI scrib " S TEXT"
Write up to four characters on strip
.IR S 's
scribble strip.
.TP
.BI led " NAME" : S | KEY " on" | off
Light or clear a key's LED, by name and strip (for example
.BR mute:1 )
or by key number.
.TP
.BI fader " S POS"
Move strip
.IR S 's
fader to
.I POS
(0 to 1) when no hand holds it.
.TP
.BI ring " S MASK"
Light strip
.IR S 's
V-Pot ring LEDs from a 15-bit mask; bit 0 is the leftmost LED.
.TP
.B quit
Write "OFF ", disconnect and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on
.BR quit ;
1 when the packet socket cannot be had from the helper, the FIFO cannot be opened, or the
backend does not open; 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diginet-packet-helper (1),
.BR diginet-probe (1)
